  "root_cause_narrative": "The provider gateway delivers at least once, so redelivered billing events arrive under fresh delivery_ids. makeIdempotencyKey (src/lib/keys.js) builds the dedupe key from delivery_id instead of event.id, so every redelivery passes the dedupe store and is sent again — the duplicate outbox lines share an event_id but differ in delivery_id. The send-path retry wrapper is a red herring: data/send.log contains zero send_error and zero failed lines, so retries never re-sent anything. The fix is keying on event.id (one notification per billing event) plus a regression test covering a redelivered event."
